THE REPOSITORY MUST STAY PRIVATE.

Not because of anything in the code — every line of it is the copyright
holder's own work — but because of the admin UI's visual language. It was
informed by the DashSpace admin template, licensed from Envato Elements under
item licence code 9FJS2WLKE3 (see NOTICE.md and licenses/). That licence is
commercial, worldwide and perpetual for the life of this End Product, and it
covers everything this project does with the design.

What it does not permit is redistributing the design as something others can
build from. Publishing this repository would do exactly that, whatever the
intention. Nothing else here is constrained: the repository can be shared with
employees, contractors and the servers it is deployed to, and the running
application can be used by anyone the copyright holder chooses.

See NOTICE.md for the third-party components that ship with this software and
the terms they carry.
